 ],
 "answer_text": "Found 3 gene records for Li-Fraumeni syndrome: cyclin dependent kinase inhibitor 2A [3], checkpoint kinase 2 [5] and tumor protein p53 [6], linked to 1 disease: Li-Fraumeni syndrome [4]. \n\nThese likely reflect modifier or related-pathway contributions, as phenotypic heterogeneity among carriers of the same pathogenic TP53 variant has been attributed to polymorphic variants in TP53-related genes, copy number variations, and epigenetic deregulation [1]. \n\nClinical context\n\nMedGen lists no clinical features for Li-Fraumeni syndrome [2]. \n\nDisease records found\n\nDisease name: Li-Fraumeni syndrome [4]. \n\nGene-to-disease mapping\n\nGene NCBIGene:1029, name: cyclin dependent kinase inhibitor 2A [3]. Gene NCBIGene:11200, name: checkpoint kinase 2 [5]. Gene NCBIGene:7157, name: tumor protein p53 [6]. \n\nPubmed records found\n\nPubmed title: Li-Fraumeni Syndrome [7]. Pubmed title: Li-Fraumeni syndrome [11]. Pubmed title: Li-Fraumeni Syndrome [13]. Pubmed title: Li-Fraumeni syndrome heterogeneity [15]. \n\nMedgen records found\n\nMedgen title: Li-Fraumeni syndrome [8]. Medgen clinical_features: MedGen lists no clinical features for Li-Fraumeni syndrome [2]. \n\nLiterature entity records found\n\nLiterature entity name: Li-Fraumeni Syndrome [9]. \n\nClinical trial records found\n\nClinical trial name: Clinical, Genetic, Behavioral, Laboratory and Epidemiologic Characterization of Individuals and Families at High Risk of Breast/Ovarian Cancer [10]. Clinical trial name: Role of p53 Gene in Metabolism Regulation in Patients With Li-Fraumeni Syndrome [12]. Clinical trial name: Characterization of Patients With Uncommon Presentations and/or Uncommon Diseases Associated With the Cardiovascular System [14]. Clinical trial name: Clinical and Genetic Studies of Li-Fraumeni Syndrome [16]. Clinical trial name: LIFSCREEN : Evaluation of Whole Body MRI for Early Detection of Cancers in Subjects With P53 Mutation (Li-Fraumeni Syndrome) [17]. "
